WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.640 --> 00:00:04.720
Which horror icon went back to his&nbsp;
day job after fighting the undead?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.720 --> 00:00:08.480
How does the sequel to "The&nbsp;
Shining" finish on a positive note?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:08.480 --> 00:00:12.320
These disturbing movies are known&nbsp;
for their surprisingly happy endings.

00:00:13.120 --> 00:00:18.880
Before 2017's "Get Out," Jordan Peele was known&nbsp;
for his gut-busting comedy chops in "Key &amp; Peele"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:18.880 --> 00:00:24.160
— so when he decided to helm a horror film, it&nbsp;
was a bit of a surprise. His resulting film was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.160 --> 00:00:29.600
a massive success by every metric, though.&nbsp;
Beloved by audiences and critics alike,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:29.600 --> 00:00:36.880
it earned over $255 million worldwide, and Peele&nbsp;
scored the Oscar for Best Original Screenplay.

00:00:36.880 --> 00:00:41.680
The story follows Chris, played by Daniel&nbsp;
Kaluuya, a Black man who visits his white&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:41.680 --> 00:00:47.280
girlfriend's family for the first time. Things&nbsp;
go from mildly uncomfortable to deeply unsettling&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:47.280 --> 00:00:52.640
when he discovers that they run a secret operation&nbsp;
that transfers the brains of aging white people&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:52.640 --> 00:00:57.920
into young, fit bodies. Now, Chris has been&nbsp;
seduced by Rose to become their next victim.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:58.560 --> 00:01:02.480
After a terrifying visit to the&nbsp;
"sunken place," Chris fights back&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.480 --> 00:01:08.160
and dispatches his girlfriend and her family in&nbsp;
a spectacularly bloody fashion. However, a final&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:08.160 --> 00:01:13.840
moment of tension arises when, during Chris'&nbsp;
bloody escape, he sees flashing lights ahead.

00:01:13.840 --> 00:01:18.640
Those well-versed in horror history, not&nbsp;
to mention centuries of racial injustice,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:18.640 --> 00:01:23.360
might reasonably expect a tragic ending&nbsp;
where our hero is arrested or gunned down.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:23.920 --> 00:01:30.480
Fortunately, the vehicle is driven by Chris' TSA&nbsp;
agent friend Rod, played by Lil Rel Howery. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:30.480 --> 00:01:36.240
two drive off into the night, leaving the scene of&nbsp;
the grisly slaughter behind. The film even ends on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:36.240 --> 00:01:40.400
a moment of levity, with Rod telling Chris that&nbsp;
he should've listened to him in the first place.

00:01:41.360 --> 00:01:42.880
"I mean I told you not to go in that house."

00:01:47.200 --> 00:01:52.800
Danny Boyle's grungy thriller "28 Days Later" was&nbsp;
an instant genre classic when it hit theaters in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.800 --> 00:01:58.960
2002. In the film, activists free chimpanzees&nbsp;
from a lab and inadvertently release a virus&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:58.960 --> 00:02:04.480
that infects people with rage and, depending on&nbsp;
who you ask, turns them into a form of zombie.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:05.040 --> 00:02:08.480
The key difference? These&nbsp;
creatures sprint after its prey&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:08.480 --> 00:02:12.000
rather than slowly shuffling&nbsp;
like others of its cinematic ilk.

00:02:12.560 --> 00:02:17.520
Weeks after the outbreak, Jim, played by&nbsp;
Cillian Murphy, wakes up from a coma into&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:17.520 --> 00:02:22.320
a world he no longer recognizes. Before long,&nbsp;
he's teamed up with some fellow survivors as they&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:22.320 --> 00:02:28.960
attempt to reach a safe haven promised by radio&nbsp;
broadcasts. Things go from bad to worse, however,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:28.960 --> 00:02:32.240
when it turns out that the military&nbsp;
regiment sending the messages&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:32.240 --> 00:02:37.200
is trying to lure female survivors in with&nbsp;
a misguided plan to repopulate the world.

00:02:37.200 --> 00:02:42.400
Jim rescues his new friends from the twisted&nbsp;
soldiers by unleashing an infected man upon them,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:42.400 --> 00:02:48.000
and the result is a blood-soaked finale in which&nbsp;
Jim is shot. Even though they escape, surely&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:52.800
nothing but horror awaits them in a world where&nbsp;
mankind's savage nature has run this rampant,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:52.800 --> 00:02:57.520
right? Not so, as the last moments of the&nbsp;
film show the characters recovering in a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:57.520 --> 00:03:02.240
pleasant cottage and suggest that they&nbsp;
may be saved by a passing fighter jet.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:02.240 --> 00:03:06.640
Though we know that things eventually&nbsp;
go badly again in the sequel "28 Weeks&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:06.640 --> 00:03:10.720
Later," the survivors of this film seem&nbsp;
like they've gotten past the worst of it.

00:03:11.520 --> 00:03:15.440
"Ready or Not" was directed by Matt&nbsp;
Bettinelli-Olpin and Tyler Gillett&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:15.440 --> 00:03:20.160
of the filmmaking collective Radio Silence,&nbsp;
who went on to find even greater success with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:20.160 --> 00:03:25.600
their reboot of the "Scream" franchise. The&nbsp;
2019 thriller stars Samara Weaving as Grace,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:25.600 --> 00:03:28.880
a newlywed who's marrying into&nbsp;
the wealthy Le Domas family.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:28.880 --> 00:03:32.160
After the wedding, her new in-laws&nbsp;
reveal that she must participate&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:32.160 --> 00:03:37.280
in their long-standing tradition of playing a&nbsp;
game in order to officially join their ranks.

00:03:37.280 --> 00:03:42.240
Unfortunately for all involved, Grace draws&nbsp;
the card for Hide-and-Seek. It turns out the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:42.240 --> 00:03:47.680
Le Domases got their fortune through an ancient,&nbsp;
satanic pact. When a new family member draws this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:47.680 --> 00:03:52.640
card, the rest of the clan must arm themselves&nbsp;
and hunt her down in order to provide a blood&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:52.640 --> 00:03:57.840
sacrifice. This leads to a desperate quest for&nbsp;
survival as Grace looks for a way to flee their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:57.840 --> 00:04:03.520
mansion while evading her murderous in-laws. As&nbsp;
dawn approaches and the family gets more frantic,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:03.520 --> 00:04:07.440
she finds increasingly violent&nbsp;
ways to turn the tables on them.

00:04:07.440 --> 00:04:12.480
Near the end of the film, Grace is captured and&nbsp;
the remaining family members rush to finish the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:12.480 --> 00:04:18.480
blood ritual before the sun rises. However, she&nbsp;
manages to escape their clutches just in time for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:18.480 --> 00:04:24.320
the ritual to fail. Apparently, this causes all&nbsp;
the members of the family to spontaneously explode&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:24.320 --> 00:04:29.840
in a manner that's both horrific and comedic at&nbsp;
the same time. Grace sits back and relaxes as the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:29.840 --> 00:04:35.360
mansion burns behind her, having dodged a bullet&nbsp;
by not becoming part of such a deranged legacy.

00:04:35.920 --> 00:04:38.160
"Jesus Christ, what happened to you?"&nbsp;

00:04:41.520 --> 00:04:42.160
"In-laws."

00:04:42.800 --> 00:04:47.760
Based on the novel by John Ajvide Lindqvist,&nbsp;
the Swedish film "Let the Right One In" tracks&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:47.760 --> 00:04:53.120
the unique relationship between Oskar and Eli.&nbsp;
He's a 12-year-old loner who's being relentlessly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:53.120 --> 00:04:58.320
bullied, and she's the strange girl who moves into&nbsp;
his apartment building. Over time, they build a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:58.320 --> 00:05:03.200
cute friendship that seems like it could blossom&nbsp;
into something resembling young love. There's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:03.200 --> 00:05:08.640
only one wrinkle: Eli is a vampire, and has been&nbsp;
trapped in a young body for a number of years.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:08.640 --> 00:05:14.160
She's dependent on an older guardian to hunt&nbsp;
down potential victims and collect blood for her.

00:05:14.160 --> 00:05:19.040
Though the story has a sweet emotional center&nbsp;
when it concerns the bond between its young leads,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:19.040 --> 00:05:23.840
there is still a deeply disturbing undercurrent&nbsp;
to the proceedings. Eli's guardian is captured&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:23.840 --> 00:05:28.320
and arrested while attempting to procure&nbsp;
blood for her, and ends up pouring acid on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:28.320 --> 00:05:34.000
his face and jumping from a hospital window to&nbsp;
avoid compromising her safety. This leads Eli&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:34.000 --> 00:05:39.200
to have to hunt for her own food, which leads to&nbsp;
retaliation from members of the local community.

00:05:39.200 --> 00:05:44.240
Even outside of the supernatural elements, there's&nbsp;
also the problem of Oskar's desire to kill the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:44.240 --> 00:05:49.440
kids who frequently torment him. When he does&nbsp;
finally strike back, they respond by attempting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:49.440 --> 00:05:54.720
to drown him in a swimming pool. Fortunately,&nbsp;
Eli comes to his rescue and gruesomely dispatches&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:54.720 --> 00:06:00.560
them all. Despite this incredibly bloody climax,&nbsp;
the film still has time for an optimistic final&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:00.560 --> 00:06:05.840
scene featuring the two on a train, running away&nbsp;
towards their own personal "happily ever after."

00:06:06.560 --> 00:06:12.160
2020's "The Invisible Man" is a loose adaptation&nbsp;
of the H.G. Wells novel from "Insidious" and "Saw"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:12.160 --> 00:06:17.760
co-creator Leigh Whannell. The film jettisons&nbsp;
virtually everything about the original story&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:17.760 --> 00:06:22.000
outside of the core premise that a man can&nbsp;
become invisible. Rather than portraying the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:22.000 --> 00:06:26.160
events from his perspective, the film&nbsp;
instead centers on his main victim,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:26.160 --> 00:06:32.240
ex-girlfriend Cecilia, who was trapped in an&nbsp;
abusive and toxic relationship before escaping.

00:06:32.240 --> 00:06:36.000
Although she is told that her former&nbsp;
boyfriend died after she left him,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:36.000 --> 00:06:41.040
Cecilia doesn't believe that he's really gone.&nbsp;
Sure enough, she finds herself tormented by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:41.040 --> 00:06:45.520
an unseen figure who attacks her when&nbsp;
no one is looking and then disappears,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:45.520 --> 00:06:50.720
making her seem increasingly unstable. The&nbsp;
titular "Invisible Man" even goes as far as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:50.720 --> 00:06:56.640
killing Cecilia's sister and framing her for the&nbsp;
murder, which lands her in a psychiatric hospital.

00:06:56.640 --> 00:07:00.800
The kill count for this film may be low, but&nbsp;
the psychological torture its protagonist&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:00.800 --> 00:07:05.840
endures more than makes up for it. Even after&nbsp;
her ex's brother is unmasked wearing the optical&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:05.840 --> 00:07:10.880
bodysuit that grants invisibility, she still&nbsp;
feels trapped by the violent relationship.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:10.880 --> 00:07:15.680
Just when it seems like she might give in due&nbsp;
to their unborn child, she suddenly takes fate,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:15.680 --> 00:07:21.520
and the invisibility suit, into her own hands by&nbsp;
killing her abuser once and for all. She even gets&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:21.520 --> 00:07:26.400
to walk off into the proverbial sunset, after&nbsp;
her detective friend seemingly lets her off the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:26.400 --> 00:07:31.520
hook after realizing what she's done. Not a bad&nbsp;
outcome, considering all she had to go through.

00:07:32.240 --> 00:07:34.160
It sounded a lot like he killed himself."

00:07:34.720 --> 00:07:39.600
Ridley Scott's original "Alien" is a classic&nbsp;
of both the science-fiction and horror genres,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:39.600 --> 00:07:44.880
boasting innovative special effects, and an&nbsp;
atmosphere of tension and claustrophobia. Any&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:44.880 --> 00:07:50.480
potential sequel was going to have its work cut&nbsp;
out for it. Fortunately for filmgoers everywhere,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:50.480 --> 00:07:55.760
director James Cameron managed to expand the scale&nbsp;
while maintaining the intimate terror of what&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:55.760 --> 00:08:02.160
came before. The result is "Aliens," an action&nbsp;
packed masterpiece as beloved as its predecessor.

00:08:02.160 --> 00:08:08.080
Set 57 years after her initial encounter with a&nbsp;
Xenomorph, the film finds Ellen Ripley awakened&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:08.080 --> 00:08:14.560
from hypersleep just in time to assist a military&nbsp;
expedition to the now-colonized LV-426. Yes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:14.560 --> 00:08:19.440
it's the same place where the deadly species was&nbsp;
first discovered. Despite traveling with a crew&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:19.440 --> 00:08:24.400
of hardened marines, it doesn't take long for the&nbsp;
creatures to begin taking them down one by one.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:24.400 --> 00:08:29.840
Their advanced weaponry fails to protect them&nbsp;
for long, and soon only a handful are left alive.

00:08:29.840 --> 00:08:35.280
In a last-ditch attempt to rescue young Newt,&nbsp;
the colony's only living survivor, Ripley goes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:35.280 --> 00:08:40.640
head-to-head with the Xenomorph Queen, who is&nbsp;
none too thrilled to have her babies set on fire.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:40.640 --> 00:08:44.600
Their grudge match eventually results in the&nbsp;
queen being blown out of their ship's air&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:44.600 --> 00:08:49.200
lock — and suddenly, all seems right with&nbsp;
the world. The planet has been destroyed,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:49.200 --> 00:08:54.560
the aliens are all dead, and Ripley even has a&nbsp;
new surrogate daughter. The final moments of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:54.560 --> 00:08:59.920
film seem almost hopeful for the future. That is,&nbsp;
as long as you ignore the rest of the franchise.

00:08:59.920 --> 00:09:04.240
"I'm sorry, Newt."
"You don't have to be sorry. It's not your fault."

00:09:04.240 --> 00:09:09.760
"The Collection," a 2012 sequel to 2009's&nbsp;
"The Collector," comes from Patrick Melton&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:09.760 --> 00:09:14.720
and Marcus Dunstan, who wrote the "Feast"&nbsp;
trilogy and four of the "Saw" films.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:14.720 --> 00:09:18.720
It's no surprise that the first film&nbsp;
is a grisly, stomach-churning affair&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:18.720 --> 00:09:23.840
involving elaborate booby traps and insidious&nbsp;
torture methods. It follows a mysterious&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:23.840 --> 00:09:28.960
figure who kidnaps his victims for nefarious&nbsp;
purposes. The film ends with him abducting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:28.960 --> 00:09:33.360
a man named Arkin, who is inadvertently&nbsp;
released at the beginning of the sequel.

00:09:33.360 --> 00:09:38.080
This time around, we get a look at the maniac's&nbsp;
hideout, an intricate warehouse filled with all&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:38.080 --> 00:09:42.240
manner of spikes and saws. Arkin leads&nbsp;
a team of mercenaries in the hopes of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:42.240 --> 00:09:47.840
retrieving a girl named Elena, and before long,&nbsp;
the majority of them find themselves torn apart&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:47.840 --> 00:09:52.640
in increasingly gruesome ways. This is&nbsp;
to say nothing of the collection itself,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:52.640 --> 00:09:57.520
a room filled with abstract sculptures&nbsp;
constructed of preserved human body parts.

00:09:57.520 --> 00:10:02.160
In the end, only Arkin and Elena are left, and&nbsp;
though Arkin is able to get the upper hand by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:02.160 --> 00:10:07.840
throwing his nemesis into a chute, it seems like&nbsp;
he might die as the building is consumed by fire.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:07.840 --> 00:10:13.040
Fortunately, Elena is able to create a path to&nbsp;
safety by smashing up the glass cases of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:13.040 --> 00:10:18.880
collection, spilling out the water within. It's&nbsp;
a triumphant scene of survival set to rock music&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:18.880 --> 00:10:23.760
that contrasts with the grimness of the rest of&nbsp;
the film. Arkin is even able to track down and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:23.760 --> 00:10:28.800
abduct the Collector himself, with the intention&nbsp;
of making sure he can't hurt anybody else.

00:10:29.600 --> 00:10:33.840
Author Stephen King may not be the biggest&nbsp;
fan, but few adaptations of his works are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:33.840 --> 00:10:39.440
more iconic than Stanley Kubrick's "The Shining."&nbsp;
The slow-burn chiller cast a spell over decades of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:39.440 --> 00:10:45.040
movie-goers with its iconic setting and memorable&nbsp;
characters. Crafting a sequel was going to be a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:45.040 --> 00:10:50.800
tall order for any filmmaker. Enter Mike Flanagan,&nbsp;
who had already adapted King's words with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:50.800 --> 00:10:56.080
"Gerald's Game" and impressed the world with his&nbsp;
"The Haunting of Hill House" series on Netflix.

00:10:56.080 --> 00:11:01.120
Flanagan took the sequel novel, "Doctor Sleep,"&nbsp;
and was able to find a happy middle-ground between&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:01.120 --> 00:11:07.040
respecting King's writing and paying homage to the&nbsp;
beloved film. The story follows Danny Torrance,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:07.040 --> 00:11:12.240
now grown up and played by Ewan McGregor, as&nbsp;
he struggles to overcome his childhood trauma,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:12.240 --> 00:11:16.080
as well as come to terms with his&nbsp;
psychic gifts. He also becomes a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:16.080 --> 00:11:20.160
mentor of sorts to a young girl&nbsp;
with similar abilities named Abra.

00:11:20.160 --> 00:11:25.040
When she's targeted by a gang of psychic&nbsp;
vampires, Danny does what he can to protect her.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:25.040 --> 00:11:29.920
As a last resort, he takes her to the Overlook&nbsp;
Hotel, where he re-experiences the horrors of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:29.920 --> 00:11:34.320
his youth. Though he is able to unleash the&nbsp;
many spirits contained there against Rose,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:34.320 --> 00:11:39.840
he ends up sacrificing both himself and the&nbsp;
hotel, which burns to the ground as Abra&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:39.840 --> 00:11:45.760
escapes. Despite this seemingly dark conclusion,&nbsp;
Abra is later able to commune with Danny's ghost,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:45.760 --> 00:11:49.920
who tells her that everything is going to&nbsp;
be all right and to use her power for good.

00:11:51.040 --> 00:11:56.960
"Shine on, Abra Stone. You shine on."

00:11:56.960 --> 00:12:00.240
Sam Raimi's "The Evil Dead" is&nbsp;
the stuff of Hollywood legend.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:00.240 --> 00:12:07.120
Shot for a measly $375,000, it launched the&nbsp;
careers of both Raimi and star Bruce Campbell&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:07.120 --> 00:12:12.480
thanks to creative filmmaking and an unsettling&nbsp;
atmosphere. The pair reunited for "Evil Dead&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:12.480 --> 00:12:17.520
II," which utilized its improved budget to&nbsp;
create even more scares and gore effects,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:17.520 --> 00:12:22.400
as well as introducing a darkly comedic tone.&nbsp;
Ash Williams may have been fighting for his life&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:22.400 --> 00:12:27.360
against the souls of the damned, but his plight&nbsp;
still managed to be downright wacky at times.

00:12:27.360 --> 00:12:32.880
This trajectory accelerated even further with&nbsp;
the third film, "Army of Darkness," which sees&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:32.880 --> 00:12:37.920
Ash transported to the Middle Ages and leading&nbsp;
a band of medieval warriors against the horrors&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:37.920 --> 00:12:43.520
of the dead. Admittedly, this is the silliest of&nbsp;
the trilogy, with several moments lifted directly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:43.520 --> 00:12:48.960
from "The Three Stooges." Even with the lighter&nbsp;
tone, it still has plenty of disturbing content,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:48.960 --> 00:12:52.800
including the army of skeletons&nbsp;
led by Ash's evil doppelganger,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:52.800 --> 00:12:58.320
whose skin has been removed from his face&nbsp;
entirely, leading to a fearsomely gruesome visage.

00:12:58.320 --> 00:13:03.360
Though many lives are lost, Ash is ultimately&nbsp;
successful at defeating evil and returning to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:03.360 --> 00:13:08.240
the present day. In a humorous epilogue, he&nbsp;
has returned to his department store job,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:08.240 --> 00:13:13.520
and even though Deadites still show up to attack&nbsp;
him, he's always ready with his trusty boomstick.

